# Component 0 is the unit square in z=0. Component 1 is a rectangle in the
# plane y=2 whose projection collapses onto the single segment (2,2)-(8,2):
# both of its "vertical" edges project to points, and its two long edges are
# collinear and completely overlapping. Component 1's edge at (2,2) passes
# through the interior of component 0's disk exactly once.
note = a two-component link whose second component projects to a segment
knot = Hopf link (linking number +/-1 by construction)
vertical_edges       == 2
collinear_overlap    >= 1
transversal          == 2
max_point_multiplicity >= 3
spatial              == 0
